Z||000000||SloPonti||01-15-2000||04:36 PM||||i got the motor back in the car today! it was a piece of cake!!! as you know i have bought the header for this motor and people who already have it on the four banger have emailed me and warned me about the header being to close to the starter solenoid! i think i have a fix for this! i made a custom heat sheild to fix this along with the help of my father! check out the pictures! also the last picture is a photo of my fiero with pure raw power! twin turbo BS ers!<BR>it is actualy me and my dad! he has helped me with this project!<BR>let me know what you guys think!!!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob<BR> <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/my55ride/engine01.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/my55ride/engine01.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/my55ride/engine02.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/my55ride/engine02.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/my55ride/engine03.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/my55ride/engine03.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/my55ride/engine04.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/my55ride/engine04.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/my55ride/air.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/my55ride/air.jpg</A> <p>[This message has been edited by SloPonti (edited 01-15-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||Patrick||01-15-2000||04:58 PM||||<BR>My gawd, you don't look old enough to drive! From the looks of your father, I've probably got a couple of years on him too. Suddenly I feel terribly old. Time for a nap.<P>Oh, by the way, the engine looks great. The heat shield around the starter should help keep it cool. Just make sure that it's well secured so that it doesn't vibrate against anything.<P>That last picture of you and your Dad is one that you'll treasure years from now. ||||reg||14
